{"type":"text","id":"ft_p","x":40,"y":2082,"width":1530,"height":50,"strokeColor":"#94a3b8","text":"[16] The Permission Ladder: two rungs in one table — local commands run, cluster commands are printed — and the printed list includes a write, so the rung is a label\n[17] Blast-Radius Gating: the destructive restart test is the change the card says to gate before, filed under checking after\n[19] Scope Lock and Checkpoint Delivery: per-workstream gates a checkpoint can cite — the stale-glob and stub gates are evidence that does not belong to this sprint's scope","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":285052},
{"type":"text","id":"ft_g","x":40,"y":2156,"width":1530,"height":35,"strokeColor":"#94a3b8","text":"prototype: a fabricated repository at the start of a sprint, the shell replaced by a stub that prints; --audit reports eight findings, from the unread plan to the pod deletion\nno shell · no cluster · only the gates that carry a finding · the recorded lint exit code is chosen to fail","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":285053}

